# --- Brand-protection domain -------------------------------------------------
# musclemetamatrix.com is an alias on the same Netlify site. Netlify does NOT
# redirect aliases to the primary domain on its own — it serves the site at
# both, which is duplicate content. These rules force the 301.
# The trailing ! makes the redirect win even though a matching file exists.

http://musclemetamatrix.com/*       https://muscle-meta.com/:splat   301!
https://musclemetamatrix.com/*      https://muscle-meta.com/:splat   301!
http://www.musclemetamatrix.com/*   https://muscle-meta.com/:splat   301!
https://www.musclemetamatrix.com/*  https://muscle-meta.com/:splat   301!

# Legacy Netlify sites → new homes.
# Add one line per old site AFTER that path exists here, then set the old
# site's own _redirects to point at muscle-meta.com.
#
# Format:  /old-path   /new-path   301
#
# Planned:
# (from osteosarcopenia-course.netlify.app)  /*  https://muscle-meta.com/courses/osteosarcopenia/:splat  301
# (from mm-mitochondrial-guide.netlify.app)  /*  https://muscle-meta.com/tools/mitochondria/:splat      301
# (from mm-vo2max-calculator.netlify.app)    /*  https://muscle-meta.com/tools/vo2max/:splat            301

# SPA-style fallback is deliberately NOT set — every page is a real file.
